      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SAISOKU (1) earns top billing after consecutive Bunbury seconds around 2000m, the better of them a nose defeat behind Major Magnus before he was again solid when second to Forever Victorious. A slight tinker with his gear should help and he can go one better to land the prize this time. POPPY'S ROSES (4) is the obvious danger after being beaten a nose as odds-on favourite at this track. CJP sticks with her as she steps right out in trip, but that doesn't look an issue third-up and she can make her presence felt. MYSTACHEENO (2) was close behind SAISOKU two back, then had a bump at the start before finishing fourth at Bunbury. Ticking along well enough to suggest he can feature. SHE'S SOME CRAIC (6) has recent efforts at this venue that keep her in the mix. SHE'SATROOPER (5) is next best.",
